# Repo understanding uses layered-explain

When the user asks how something in this repository works, wants a walkthrough, or is building understanding of existing code from scratch, read and follow `.agents/skills/layered-explain/SKILL.md`.

Trigger phrases include "how does X work", "explain X", "walk me through X", "help me understand X", and similar.

Do not use the pstack `how` or `why` skills for these questions. Those dump facts and names before the reader has a reason to care. `layered-explain` starts from the goal and ideal flow, then grows the picture by naming problems and what the code does about them.

`why` is still fine when the user is asking for design rationale, history, or motivation rather than a from-scratch understanding of the current code.
